<section class="story" id="story" aria-labelledby="story-title"><div class="story-meta">02 / A SHORT NOTE</div><article><p class="story-kicker">How I work</p><h2 id="story-title">Good software<br /><em>gets out of the way.</em></h2><p>I believe the best digital products are built at the intersection of care and curiosity. The code matters, but so does the question behind it: does this make someone's day a little clearer, faster, or more enjoyable?</p><p>I'm Juan, a software engineer who turns rough ideas into thoughtful, resilient interfaces. I care about the quiet details — the hierarchy that makes a page easy to scan, the interaction that feels natural on the first try, and the performance that gets out of the way.</p><p>I'm currently building product full time and looking for a world-class team that values craft, ownership, and a healthy amount of play.</p><p class="story-signoff">With curiosity,<br />Juan Araujo</p></article></section>
